/* @lc app=leetcode id=4003 lang=kotlin */ class Solution { fun minCost(m: Int, n: Int, penalty: Array<IntArray>): Long = LongArray(m * n * 2) { Long.MAX_VALUE }.let { dist -> java.util.PriorityQueue<LongArray>(compareBy<LongArray> { it[0] }).let { pq -> dist.set(0, 0L).also { pq.add(longArrayOf(0L, 0L)) }.let { generateSequence { pq.poll() }.forEach { (d, s) -> if (d == dist[s.toInt()]) (s.toInt() / 2).let { c -> (s.toInt() % 2).let { p -> (c / n).let { i -> (c % n).let { j -> (listOf(Triple(i, j, penalty[i][j].toLong())) + listOf(0 to 1, 1 to 0, 0 to -1, -1 to 0).withIndex().filter { (_, dd) -> i + dd.first in 0 until m && j + dd.second in 0 until n }.map { (k, dd) -> Triple(i + dd.first, j + dd.second, (i + dd.first + 1).toLong() * (j + dd.second + 1) + (if ((k < 2) == (p == 0)) 0 else penalty[i][j])) }).forEach { (a, b, w) -> ((a * n + b) * 2 + 1 - p).also { ns -> if (d + w < dist[ns]) dist.set(ns, d + w).also { pq.add(longArrayOf(d + w, ns.toLong())) } } } } } } } }.let { 1 + minOf(dist[(m * n - 1) * 2], dist[(m * n - 1) * 2 + 1]) } } } } }